From: Automation Platform controller <controller@pipefail.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 0006] the deletion pump retries FAILED deletions, not just stuck ones

Robustness fix in our own org-deletion subsystem (ADR-0001), found by a
fault-path review after the parity sweep: the pump re-dispatched pending and
stuck (cancelling/reaping >10min) deletions, but never `failed` ones. An
explicit DELETE that failed once (e.g. a job that would not cancel in the
grace window -> RuntimeError -> failed) had no caller re-issuing it and sat
stranded forever, contradicting the ADR contract ("resumable, never abort").
Lease-expiry deletions self-healed via a fresh record; explicit ones did not.

The pump now retries failed deletions on the same 10-minute backoff as stuck
ones (the reaper already transitions failed->pending at its top, so the
re-dispatch re-enters the machine cleanly). Permanent failures retry visibly
-- the record shows state=failed with its error between attempts -- rather
than silently stranding, consistent with how stuck reaps already retry.

Tested by: unit (failed->pending resumability) + tripwire baseline.

diff --git a/awx/main/tasks/org_deletion.py b/awx/main/tasks/org_deletion.py
index ef39912..adf9b7c 100644
--- a/awx/main/tasks/org_deletion.py
+++ b/awx/main/tasks/org_deletion.py
@@ -114,7 +114,17 @@ def process_organization_deletions():
     stuck = OrganizationDeletion.objects.filter(
         state__in=(OrganizationDeletion.STATE_CANCELLING_JOBS, OrganizationDeletion.STATE_REAPING), modified__lt=stale
     )
-    for deletion in list(ready) + list(stuck):
+    # A failed deletion must not strand: an explicit DELETE that failed (e.g. a
+    # job that would not cancel in the window) has no caller re-issuing it, and
+    # the ADR's contract is "resumable, never abort". Retry failed deletions on
+    # the same backoff as stuck ones — the reaper's failed->pending transition
+    # re-enters the machine. Permanent failures keep retrying visibly (the
+    # record shows state=failed with its error between attempts) rather than
+    # silently stranding, matching how stuck reaps already retry without a cap.
+    failed = OrganizationDeletion.objects.filter(
+        state=OrganizationDeletion.STATE_FAILED, modified__lt=stale
+    )
+    for deletion in list(ready) + list(stuck) + list(failed):
         logger.info('dispatching reaper for organization deletion %s (state=%s)', deletion.pk, deletion.state)
         reap_organization.apply_async([deletion.pk], queue=get_task_queuename())
 
diff --git a/awx/main/tests/unit/test_org_deletion.py b/awx/main/tests/unit/test_org_deletion.py
index 41173b3..a6bedef 100644
--- a/awx/main/tests/unit/test_org_deletion.py
+++ b/awx/main/tests/unit/test_org_deletion.py
@@ -68,3 +68,15 @@ def test_expired_lease_exclusion_states_cover_all_nonterminal():
         OrganizationDeletion.STATE_CANCELLING_JOBS,
         OrganizationDeletion.STATE_REAPING,
     }
+
+
+def test_reaper_resumes_from_failed_state():
+    # a failed deletion re-dispatched by the pump must be resumable: the reaper
+    # transitions it back to pending before proceeding (proven by the transition
+    # table allowing failed->pending and nothing else out of failed).
+    d = _unsaved(OrganizationDeletion.STATE_FAILED)
+    d.transition(OrganizationDeletion.STATE_PENDING)
+    assert d.state == OrganizationDeletion.STATE_PENDING
+    # and from pending it can proceed
+    d.transition(OrganizationDeletion.STATE_CANCELLING_JOBS)
+    assert d.state == OrganizationDeletion.STATE_CANCELLING_JOBS
